## Section bounds, overflow and demo (temporary same-origin probe)

A temporary probe page served from the worktree root (removed before the commit, not part of the
deliverable) loaded the preview in same-origin iframes at 1440×900 and 390×844 and measured the page:

```
desktop viewport=1440x900 scrollWidth=1425 clientWidth=1425 bodyScrollWidth=1425 pageHeight=6732 contractTop=953 contractBottom=2555 contractHeight=1603 contractWidth=1136 chips=31 errors=7 links=3 demoCardMoved=true demoStatus=Zoom 110 percent. zoomScale=1.10 masthead=Last change: P1-07 — Contract overview in the preview | 2026-10-25 13:57 (Europe/Zurich) firstFact=0.1.0
mobile viewport=390x844 scrollWidth=375 clientWidth=375 bodyScrollWidth=375 pageHeight=11634 contractTop=1195 contractBottom=4408 contractHeight=3213 contractWidth=343 chips=31 errors=7 links=3
tall viewport=1440x3400 scrollWidth=1425 clientWidth=1425 bodyScrollWidth=1425 pageHeight=6732 contractTop=953 contractBottom=2555 contractHeight=1603 contractWidth=1136 chips=31 errors=7 links=3
```

What the probe proves:

- **No horizontal overflow:** `scrollWidth` equals `clientWidth` at 1440 (1425) and 390 (375);
  `bodyScrollWidth` matches too, so the page is readable at both sizes.
- **The section counts are the contract's:** 31 chips = 19 operation chips + 6 client-to-server and
  6 server-to-client sync chips, plus 7 error rows and 3 document links. The facts strip states
  16 schema files (10 board content, 1 sync, 5 REST API), 19 operation types, 6 + 6 sync message
  types, 7 error codes and 77 parity fixtures (32 valid, 45 invalid).
- **The demo still works:** an `ArrowRight` press moves card A (`demoCardMoved=true`) and a click on
  the zoom-in segment moves the world layer to scale 1.10. Demo markup and `preview.js` are unchanged.
- **The masthead is refreshed:** last change `P1-07 — Contract overview in the preview`, date/time
  `2026-10-25 13:57 (Europe/Zurich)` (the change entry's modification time).

